 ["h2", "shin-splints", "Shin splints (medial tibial stress syndrome)", "Shin splints (medial tibial stress syndrome)"],
 ["p", "Shin splints adalah nyeri di sepanjang sisi dalam tulang kering, sering pada pelari yang baru menaikkan volume atau berpindah ke permukaan keras [3]. Tinjauan sistematis menemukan faktor risiko antara lain riwayat shin splints sebelumnya, indeks massa tubuh lebih tinggi, dan navicular drop (lengkung kaki yang turun berlebihan saat menumpu) [4].",
  "Shin splints are pain along the inner edge of the shinbone, common in runners who have just increased volume or moved to harder surfaces [3]. A systematic review found risk factors including a previous history of shin splints, higher body mass index and navicular drop (the arch dropping excessively under load) [4]."],
 ["p", "Satu hal yang tidak boleh dilewatkan: bila nyeri terasa di satu titik kecil yang sangat nyeri ditekan, memburuk setiap lari, atau terasa bahkan saat istirahat dan malam hari, itu perlu diperiksa untuk kemungkinan stress fracture [3].",
  "One thing not to miss: if pain sits at one small spot that is very tender to press, worsens every run, or is present even at rest and at night, it needs checking for a possible stress fracture [3]."],

 ["h2", "achilles", "Tendinopati Achilles", "Achilles tendinopathy"],
 ["p", "Tendinopati Achilles terasa sebagai nyeri dan kaku di tendon di atas tumit, khas terasa paling kaku saat langkah pertama di pagi hari atau di awal lari, lalu membaik setelah pemanasan [8]. Pedoman praktik klinis terbaru dari American Physical Therapy Association merekomendasikan latihan beban progresif sebagai inti penanganan [5].",
  "Achilles tendinopathy is pain and stiffness in the tendon above the heel, typically stiffest on the first steps in the morning or at the start of a run, then easing once warm [8]. The latest American Physical Therapy Association clinical practice guideline recommends progressive loading exercise as the core of treatment [5]."],
 ["p", "Kabar baik untuk pelari: uji klinis Silbernagel dan rekan menunjukkan pasien yang tetap berolahraga dengan \"model pemantauan nyeri\" — nyeri saat aktivitas maksimal 5/10 dan harus reda keesokan paginya — tidak mengalami hasil yang lebih buruk dibanding yang berhenti total [6]. Di Physio8 kami biasanya memulai lebih konservatif, di sekitar 3/10.",
  "Good news for runners: a clinical trial by Silbernagel and colleagues showed patients who kept exercising with a 'pain-monitoring model' — pain during activity no higher than 5/10 and settled by the next morning — did no worse than those who stopped completely [6]. At Physio8 we usually start more conservatively, around 3/10."],
